{"name":"Absinthe Dreams","hex":"#7f8b30","fetched":"2026-10-19","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"absinthe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The herb absinthium Artemisia absinthium (grande wormwood); essence of wormwood. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Bitterness; sorrow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/absinthe"},{"term":"dreams","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of dream"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of dream"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dreams"}],"entries":[{"title":"Absinthe","blocks":[{"text":"Absinthe is an anise-flavoured spirit derived from several plants, including the flowers and leaves of Artemisia absinthium, together with green anise, sweet fennel, and other medicinal and culinary herbs. Historically described as a highly alcoholic spirit, it is 45–74% ABV or 90–148 proof in the US. Absinthe traditionally has a natural green colour but may also be colourless. It is commonly referred to in historical literature as la fée verte 'the green fairy'. While sometimes casually referred to as a liqueur, absinthe is not traditionally bottled with sugar or sweeteners. Absinthe is traditionally bottled at a high level of alcohol by volume, but it is normally diluted with water before being consumed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Absinthe-glass.jpg/330px-Absinthe-glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Absinthe","wikidata":"Q170210"},{"title":"Dream","blocks":[{"text":"A dream is a succession of images, dynamic scenes and situations, ideas, emotions, and sensations that usually occur involuntarily in the mind during certain stages of sleep. Humans generally spend more than two hours dreaming per night, and each dream lasts around 5–20 minutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg/330px-A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dream","wikidata":"Q36348"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Absinthe-glass.jpg/330px-Absinthe-glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Absinthe-glass.jpg/330px-Absinthe-glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAbsinthe-glass.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Albert_Maignan_-_La_muse_verte.jpg/250px-Albert_Maignan_-_La_muse_verte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/75/Albert_Maignan_-_La_muse_verte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Albert_Maignan_-_La_muse_verte.jpg/250px-Albert_Maignan_-_La_muse_verte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Albert Maignan's Green Muse (1895): a poet succumbs to the Green Fairy.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlbert_Maignan_-_La_muse_verte.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Absinthe_Frapp%C3%A9.jpg/500px-Absinthe_Frapp%C3%A9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Absinthe_Frapp%C3%A9.jpg/1280px-Absinthe_Frapp%C3%A9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Absinthe_Frapp%C3%A9.jpg/500px-Absinthe_Frapp%C3%A9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbna